DAY 6: BASIC MATH / PREREQUISITES (STATISTICS / PROBABILITY INTRO)

MEAN : AVERAGE VALUE OF A FEATURE
MEDIAN : MIDDLE VALUE (ROBUST TO OUTLIERS).
MODE : MOST FREQUENT VALUE.
VARIANCE AND STANDARD DEVIATION : SPREAD OF DATA.

DISTRIBUTIONS (HIGH LEVEL)
	1. Normal distribution : bell curve, symmetric around mean.
	2. Skewed distributions: long tail on one side (common in real data).

Why stats matter for ML
	1. Helps understand data (EDA).
	2. Helps choose transformations (log, scaling, etc.).
	3. Helps interpret model assumptions (e.g., linear regression).
	4. Probability basics
	5. Event, probability of an event.

1.	Insance Based learning

2.	Model Based Learning
