Day 13 : End - to - End Toy Project


Steps : 
	0. Preprocessing + EDA + feature selection
	1. Extract input and output columns
	2. Scale the values
	3. train_test_split
	4. train model
	5. evaluate model / model selection
	6. Deploy model

Load Data
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_csv('file_path.csv')
df.head()
df.shape
df = df.iloc[:, 1:]

Visualize data
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
plt.scatter(df['cgpa'], df['iq'], c = df['placement'])

Input, output extraction
X = df.iloc[:, 0:2]
y = df.iloc(:, -1]

Splitting of data for training and testing
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test = train_test_split(X_train, y_train, test_size = 0.1)

Scaling values
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler
scaler = StandardScaler()
X_train = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)
X_test = scaler.fit_transform(X_test)

Model training
from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression
clf.fit(X_train, y_train)

y_pred = clf.predict(X_test)

Evaluation of model
from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score
acccuracy = accuracy_score(y_pred, y_test)

Visualize decision boundaries
from mlxtend.plotting import plot_decision_regions
plot_decision_regions((X_train, y_train.values, clf = clf, legend = 2)

make model pickle file
import pickle
pickle.dump(clf, open('model.pkl', 'wb'))

then it will be integrated with website and deployed through GCP, AWS, VERCEL,etc

